title: 'Transfer on-demand coretime revenue to the broker pallet locally'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-on-demand-para` now books the revenue from the on-demand coretime orders it
    sells, and hands it over to `pallet-broker`, replicating what the Relay Chain's
    on-demand pallet does for the Coretime chain today.

    The spot price paid for an order is kept in the pallet's pot and booked against
    the timeslice the order was placed in, which the pallet derives from the new
    `TimeslicePeriod` config item. That must match the `TimeslicePeriod` of
    `pallet-broker`. The unclaimed revenue of at most `MaxUnclaimedTimeslices` (a new
    config item) timeslices is kept apart; beyond that, the revenue of the oldest
    timeslice is merged into the next oldest one.

    `pallet-broker` claims that revenue through the new `OnDemandRevenue` trait in
    `fp-coretime`, which `pallet-on-demand-para` implements, and which its new
    `OnDemandRevenue` config item names. Once a timeslice ends, `pallet-broker` claims
    the revenue of that timeslice and of every earlier timeslice not claimed yet, and
    gets the amount paid out for each timeslice back, so the revenue is attributed
    correctly even while the broker is catching up with timeslices after the chain has
    stalled. The revenue of a timeslice is only paid out in full, oldest first. If the
    pot happens to hold less than the revenue booked, the revenue of as many timeslices
    as it can cover is paid out, an `UnexpectedLowFunds` event is emitted, and the rest
    stays booked until the pot has been topped up. Revenue which is not paid out, for
    this or any other reason, is claimed along with a later timeslice, and `pallet-broker`
    keeps the history of the ended timeslice until then.

    Since both pallets live on the same chain there is no need for XCM: the funds are
    transferred straight into the broker pot, and the revenue is distributed among the
    contributors to the Instantaneous Coretime Pool within the same block. This replaces
    the round-trip in which the Relay Chain teleports the revenue to the Coretime chain
    and reports it with `notify_revenue`, so the payouts are ready one block earlier than
    they used to be.

    On-demand coretime sales in `pallet-on-demand-para` are disabled until they are enabled
    with the new `enable` call, which requires Root or `AdminOrigin`, is free, and emits an
    `Enabled` event. Once enabled, they cannot be disabled again, and calling `enable` again
    does nothing. Until they are enabled, `place_order` fails with the new `Disabled` error,
    so no revenue is booked which would never be distributed.

    `pallet-broker` follows that switch through the new `OnDemandRevenue::is_enabled`. Until
    the on-demand market is enabled, `pallet-broker` behaves as before: it requests the
    revenue from the Relay Chain with `CoretimeInterface::request_revenue_info_at` and
    distributes what the Relay Chain reports with `notify_revenue`. Once it is enabled,
    `pallet-broker` only claims the revenue locally, makes no requests to the Relay Chain,
    and ignores the `RevenueInbox`. Runtimes which keep requesting the revenue from the
    Relay Chain can set `OnDemandRevenue` to `()`, which is never enabled.

    `pallet-on-demand-para` is also wired into the coretime-westend runtime. It starts out
    disabled, so the broker keeps requesting the revenue from the Relay Chain until on-demand
    coretime sales are enabled with `enable`, without a runtime upgrade.

    With the `runtime-benchmarks` feature enabled, `PoolCapacityProvider` has a new
    `ensure_pool_cores` method, which the benchmarks use to make sure the pool is not
    empty before they place orders, and `QueueOnDemandOrders` has a new
    `ensure_successful_delivery` method, which makes sure the batch of orders sent on
    finalization reaches the Relay Chain.
crates:
- name: fp-coretime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: major
- name: pallet-on-demand-para
  bump: major
- name: coretime-westend-runtime
  bump: major
